<p>{{ article.excerpt }}</p><h2>Start with noticing</h2><p>Pay attention to the small decisions that make a practice your own. A thoughtful first observation can be more useful than a perfect plan.</p><blockquote>Good work begins with a little room to be curious.</blockquote><h2>Make room for the process</h2><p>Protect a small space, ask a clear question and invite another perspective.</p><ul><li>Choose one question worth exploring.</li><li>Make a visible first attempt.</li><li>Listen before refining.</li></ul><h2>Carry one idea forward</h2><p>The next thoughtful step is often enough. Try it for a week and notice what changes.</p>
